   "PDAG": "Partially directed acyclic graph, allowing both directed and undirected edges. SHD is defined over these, which is why it covers DAGs as a special case.",
   "d-separation": "A purely graphical test for whether conditioning on a set blocks every path between two nodes. Blocks chains and forks at a conditioned node, and opens a collider when the collider or one of its descendants is conditioned on.",
   "collider": "A node with two arrowheads into it on a path. Blocked by default, and opened by conditioning on it or on any of its descendants -- the reverse of every other node's behaviour.",
